          "title": "Double Exposure Blackjack",
          "subtitle": "Gambling",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Double Exposure Blackjack is a blackjack variant where both dealer cards are dealt face-up, offset by rule changes that preserve the house edge."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "A casino blackjack variant also known as Zweikartenspiel, designed around the unusual information advantage of seeing the dealer hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "1-7 against dealer players use the table arrangement described for Double Exposure Blackjack."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Multiple standard 52-card decks"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Multiple standard 52-card decks, score area, and enough table space for play."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Deal two exposed dealer cards and two player cards to each betting position."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
